{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-boundary parity contract for the web->native export-options mapping.",
    "Single source of truth shared by BOTH sides of the export IPC:",
    "  - web:    buildNativeExportOptions() in src/composables/timeline/export/core/useExportProcess.ts",
    "  - native: NativeExportOptions (serde, camelCase) in src-tauri/src/media/timeline_export/options.rs",
    "Each side has a test that reads this file:",
    "  - TS   asserts buildNativeExportOptions(webInput) deep-equals `native`.",
    "  - Rust asserts `native` deserializes into NativeExportOptions with the same typed values.",
    "So a rename/retype on EITHER side (a web key change or a Rust field/serde change) breaks a test",
    "instead of silently dropping an export option over the wire.",
    "",
    "KNOWN INTENTIONAL DIVERGENCE: the web side emits `videoMinBitrateBps`, but NativeExportOptions",
    "has no matching field, so serde silently drops it — native export never applies a minimum bitrate.",
    "The `native` blocks below still carry the web-produced `videoMinBitrateBps` (to pin the TS output),",
    "but the Rust test does NOT assert it (there is nothing to deserialize it into). See case",
    "`mp4_cbr_metadata_advanced`, whose non-zero min bitrate is dropped natively."
  ],
